---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Docs — Tempo"
  description="Integration guides and how-to documentation for Tempo: Home Assistant, score authoring, troubleshooting."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <nav class="page-nav">
      <a href="/">← tempoapp.app</a>
    </nav>
    <h1>Documentation</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Integration guides and how-tos. Each page is self-contained and
      written for somebody who has Tempo running on their Mac and a
      specific source they want to connect.
    </p>
  </header>

  <main class="doc">

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Integration guides</h2>
      <ul class="cards">
        <li class="card">
          <a href="/docs/home-assistant">
            <h3>Home Assistant</h3>
            <p>
              Send any HA state change, automation completion, or system
              event to Tempo. Five-minute setup, copy-paste cookbook for
              safety sensors, doors, locks, alarm panels, climate, presence,
              and automations.
            </p>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="more-coming">
        More integration guides land here as Tempo's source list grows —
        Kopia, UniFi, Uptime Kuma, Synology, Pi-hole, Proxmox, GitHub
        Actions and the rest already work today via the
        <a href="/scores">bundled scores</a>; dedicated guides arrive in
        the post-launch updates.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Reference</h2>
      <ul class="cards">
        <li class="card">
          <a href="/scores">
            <h3>Scores catalogue</h3>
            <p>
              Browse the bundled and community scores — pre-configured
              event recipes for common sources, double-click to install.
            </p>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <a href="/scores/troubleshooting-networking">
            <h3>Troubleshooting networking</h3>
            <p>
              Five patterns that cover almost every "score installed but
              nothing arrives in Tempo" situation: firewall, Little Snitch,
              VLAN isolation, hostname resolution, port collision.
            </p>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

  </main>

  <style>
    .page-header {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 48px auto 24px;
      padding: 0 24px;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .page-nav {
      font-size: 14px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    .page-nav a {
      color: var(--blue);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .page-header h1 {
      font-size: 36px;
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 16px 20px;
      background: var(--bg2);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .doc {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0 auto 80px;
      padding: 0 24px;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .doc .group {
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
    .doc h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      color: var(--text);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .cards {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 16px 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    @media (min-width: 720px) {
      .cards {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      }
    }
    .card {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: var(--bg2);
      transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
    }
    .card:hover {
      border-color: var(--blue);
    }
    .card a {
      display: block;
      padding: 16px 20px;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-size: 17px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .card p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text2);
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .more-coming {
      color: var(--text2);
      font-size: 14px;
      margin-top: 16px;
    }
    .more-coming a {
      color: var(--blue);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
